---
import EvidenceBundleInspector from "../components/EvidenceBundleInspector.astro";
import HeaderInspector from "../components/HeaderInspector.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Offline deployment assessment"
  description="Assess bounded, subject-identified response, HTML resource, request-context, and reduced WebAuthn evidence locally."
>
  <header class="shell page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">Configuration evidence without scanning</span>
    <h1>Inspect deployment evidence offline</h1>
    <p>
      Move beyond feature availability by checking response policies, route variation, SRI
      declarations, Fetch Metadata request context, and reduced WebAuthn configuration against
      explicit per-surface requirements. Reduced reports bind an opaque application, environment,
      revision, producer, capture window, and privacy-minimised scope inventory into their
      fingerprint. An optional CLI gate can verify an externally signed Sigstore statement from one
      exact policy-selected workflow identity. Neither path discovers routes, certifies a site, or
      replaces runtime testing.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="shell">
    <HeaderInspector />
    <EvidenceBundleInspector />
    <aside class="content-card">
      <span class="eyebrow">Optional authenticated provenance</span>
      <h2>Verify the exported report in CI</h2>
      <p>
        The browser inspector deliberately remains unsigned and offline. After export, the CLI can
        create one canonical in-toto statement over the report fingerprint, deployment identity, and
        reduced scope inventory. A separately reviewed CI workflow can sign that statement as a
        Sigstore DSSE bundle.
      </p>
      <p>
        <code>verify-evidence</code> checks the signature, trusted certificate, transparency evidence,
        exact issuer and workflow identity, report digest, and deployment predicate before applying the
        independent evidence policy. Complete bundles and certificates are not retained in the reduced
        result.
      </p>
      <p>
        A verified statement authenticates the configured signer and matching report. It does not
        prove that evidence collection was complete, truthful, or representative of runtime
        enforcement.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
